OL,3,GNEWSAConcerns raised over island's food
OL,4,Asecurity
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former politician has raised concerns
OL,7,Fover Jersey school meals being supplied
OL,8,Fby a UK company, suggesting it raises
OL,9,Fwider concerns about the island's food
OL,10,Fsecurity and resilience.
OL,12,FFormer deputy David Warr said there was
OL,13,F"no local firm" which could produce the
OL,14,Fvolume of meals required for schools in
OL,15,Fthe island - UK company Apetito was
OL,16,Frecently appointed.
OL,18,F"If we can't even feed 9,000 kids, what
OL,19,Fthe hell chance have we got of feeding
OL,20,F104,000 people on this island if that
OL,21,Ffood isn't available?," he said.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,444,440,260,160,0,100
